-- Playground example: an argument passed straight through a call.
-- Drawn with call panels (once jl4-lsp sends call expansions; specified 2026-10-05, not yet landed),
-- in `pass through` the `a` inside the `limb a b` panel IS the caller's own `a`,
-- and in `record pass through` the inlined `a's has stable income` IS the direct one,
-- so one click answers both boxes.
-- Not a corpus file: nothing goldens it. Its job is to exercise the ladder playground.

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb` p q IF p AND q

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `pass through` a b IF
      `limb` a b
  AND a

DECLARE Person
  HAS `has stable income`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `has recent default`  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is creditworthy` p IF
      p's `has stable income`
  AND NOT p's `has recent default`

GIVEN a IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `record pass through` a IF
      `is creditworthy` a
  AND a's `has stable income`
